Generate work for a 32-byte block hash (hex encoded)

Usage: nano-rspow generate [OPTIONS] [HASH]

Arguments:
  [HASH]
          Block root hash (64 hex chars). Optional if --stream is used

Options:
      --stream
          Run in stdio streaming mode.
          
          Reads newline-delimited requests from stdin and writes results to stdout. Empty lines are ignored.
          
          INPUT  (one request per line, threshold is optional): <hash_hex>:<threshold_hex>   — per-request threshold (0x prefix required) <hash_hex>                   — uses --threshold (or the default)
          
          OUTPUT (one result per line, same order): <hash_hex>:<threshold_hex>:<nonce_hex> e.g.  718cc2121c3e641059bc1c2cfc45666c99e8ae922f7a807b7d07b62c995d79e2:0xfffffff800000000:2bf29ef00786a6bc
          
          ERRORS are written to stderr; the offending line is skipped and processing continues. Cancellation also goes to stderr.
          
          NOTES: - Per-line <threshold_hex> must include the 0x prefix. - The process exits cleanly when stdin is closed (EOF).

  -t, --threshold <THRESHOLD>
          Difficulty threshold (hex, default: current send/change)
          
          [default: fffffff800000000]

  -b, --backend <BACKEND>
          Backend to use: cpu, gpu, opencl
          
          [default: gpu]

      --retune
          For GPU backend: bypass cache and run dispatch tuning probe

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
